<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds were swept higher in the wake of a rally in U.S. Treasuries and a strong dollar in afternoon trade on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>If Treasuries and the U.S. currency remain strong, traders said they expected to see further gains in bonos.</p>
<p>&quot;Bonos underperformed last week and now investors are seeing some value, but traders will also be keeping an eye on the peseta which is rapidly weakening,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>The peseta slipped to 84.40/43 in late trade compared with levels seen late on Monday of 83.13/14.</p>
</text>
